{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (Semir Poturak / the Svemir system as \"matica\") assigned a numismatics research task (\"Zadatak: numizmatika — monetarna hronologija Medijane\") for the Medijana (Naissus/Niš, 4th c. imperial villa) 3D reconstruction database at `C:\\Svemir\\data\\sessions\\c1792946760393lb6a\\medijana_baza\\`. I am one mind in a swarm (roj_glm/numizmatika). Explicit requirements:\n   - First read `README.md`, `sonde_sloj.json`, `sobe_sloj.json`; do NOT modify existing base files\n   - Known numismatic data in base: pre-villa coins 271–275 and 294–307 (w-9); kasnolatenska fibula pre-rimski; closed contexts: 335–336 (w-9), 355–361 (w-10, 4 komada), 364–375 (w-21 → rušenje 378, Gotski rat), 364–367 (w-24a), 382–389 (w-24, posle rušenja); trem 3 komada; bronzana ograda zakopana 378. Open conflict: Vicennalia (325/6) vs Tricennalia (335/6) — \"trideset godina vladavine\" u književnosti\n   - 5 research goals: (1) coin find types at Medijana in literature (which emperors, mints, denominations); (2) Vicennalia vs Tricennalia — what are the medallions/special issues of 325/6 and 335/6, what would a find mean for dating villa phase 2; (3) monetary circulation in Moesia 350–380 — does \"youngest coin 375–378\" reliably date demolition (when does circulation cease after 378? Gothic war, Hadrianopolis); (4) coins 382–389 after demolition — Theodosius I, what they say about continued life; (5) hoard analysis — does a coin hoard from Medijana exist in museums\n   - Output in this folder (`roj_glm/numizmatika/`): `nalaz.md` and `novac.json` — an array of `{id, carevi_period, nalaz_sonda_soba_ako_ima, znacaj_za_hronologiju, izvor_url, poverenje}`\n   - End the message with a 5–10 line summary\n   - Rules: srpski, latinica; every claim with URL source and confidence; conflicts written up; no npm installations; do not commit; limitations written honestly\n   - After session crash, user said: \"Nastavi zadatak iz ZADATAK.md u ovom folderu. Nisi na početku — sesija ti je pala usred rada; nastavi tačno gde si stao koristeći već skinute izvore na disku, ne kreći ispočetka. Na kraju predaj nalaz.md.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Medijana/Mediana villa with peristyle: 3 building horizons — horizont 1 (first decades of 4th c.), horizont 2 (~330 – Gothic raids 378), horizont 3 (after 383 – Hun demolition 441/443)\n   - Coin-dating of strata: closed finds (zatvorene celine) vs single finds; stratigraphy layers A (recent), B (secondary demolition), C (roof demolition/fire), D (living level), E (protohumus/zdravica)\n   - Coin tables from Vasić–Milošević–Gavrilović, \"Iskopavanja Medijane u 2010. i 2011. godini\", Starinar LXIV/2014, 231–263 (Tabele 1a, 2a, 6, 8)\n   - Numismatic literature: Janković-Mihaldžić 2008 \"Pojedinačni nalazi rimskog novca na Medijani\", Naissus I, Niš 2008, 25–73; Janković-Mihaldžić 2001, Zbornik Narodnog muzeja Niš 10, 27–38 (novac sa objekta B)\n   - Vicennalia (VOT XX, 325/6) vs Tricennalia (VOT XXX, 335/6) of Constantine — unresolved base conflict\n   - Valens GLORIA ROMANORUM 366–367; Theodosius I coins 382–389; post-378 coin circulation cessation; Hun invasion 441\n   - Svemir system conventions: opismeni package, kosnica/roj tools, tasks in working dir, no commits unless asked, srpski latinica\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `medijana_baza/README.md` (read) — base structure v0.14/0.15: 19 3D stubova, kote 197.28–200.64 m n.m.v., najniža kota 195.96 (kasnosrednjovekovni bunar), rušenje 378 vezano na zatvorene celine novca u tremu, w-9, w-10, w-21; otvoreno: Vicennalia vs Tricennalia\n   - `medijana_baza/pdf/milosevic_iskopi.txt` (read extensively, lines 180–330, 465–590, 755–1050, 1530–1660) — THE primary source. Extracted data:\n     - Tabela 1a (severoistočni/NW sektor) — Sloj B: kota 199.47: 355-361; 199.43: 364-375; 199.44: 4. vek; 199.14: 404-406; 199.03: 4. vek + 335-337. Sloj D: 198.98: 4. vek; 198.93: 364-375; 198.91: 5. veka + 364-375 (x2); 198.89: 425-450 (ispod tegula, dno kasete); 198.86: 4. vek; 198.84: 364-367 + 364-375 (x2) + 4. vek; 198.83: 364-367; 198.79: 355-361; 198.76: 330-335; 198.69: 341-346; 198.67: 330-335; prefurnijum stibadijuma B 198.51: 364-375. Sonda 45 (w-24a) 198.96: 364-367; Sonda 46 (ulaz u stibadijum B) 198.85: 382-389\n     - Tabela 2a (NE sektor): 355-361 s.97 C 198.86; 364-375 s.97 C 198.91; 4. vek s.98 C 198.84; 355-361 s.98 C 198.76; 330-335 s.103 C 198.85; 294-307 s.104 C 198.81\n     - Tabela 6 (SW sektor 2011, w-21, sloj D): 4. vek 198.48; 364-375 ×4 (198.46 ×3, 198.45); 360-361 198.52. (2010): 364-375 s.78 prostorija 21/22 sokl 198.59; 335-336 s.75 w-9 B 198.75; 271-275 s.75 w-9 C 198.49; 355-361 ×4 s.76 w-10 B (198.52, 198.53, 198.54, 198.54)\n     - Tabela 8 (trem): 2010: 364-375 s.81 B 198.59; 367-375 s.81 B 198.59; 2011: 271 zid 49 A \"0\" (artefakt formatiranja); 355-361 trem D 198.41\n     - Skrivnica: \"U tankom sloju zemqe na dnu kasete, na koti 198.89 na|en je komad bronzanog novca iz perioda 425-450. godine... U gorwem nivou sloja D na-|ena su i dva komada novca iz perioda 382-389. godine i jo{ dva komada iz intervala 404-450. godine\" → horizont sloja D korišćen i posle 380, kraj Medijane hunski upad 441\n     - Trem closed find: \"na|eni novac iz zatvorene celine, a ve}ina pripada periodu 364-375. godine, neposredno pred prvo ru{ewe vile, koje upravo zbog ovih nalaza mo`emo da pripi{emo provali Gota posle hadrijanopoqske bitke 378. godine\"\n     - Horizonti: \"horizont 1 (prve decenije 4. veka), horizont 2 (oko 330 - do gotskih upada 378. godine) i horizont 3 (posle 383 - do provale Huna 441-443. godine)\"\n     - Footnote 14: novac \"... Val ... (Valens), a na reversu GLORIA ROMANORUM (Jankovi}-Mihald`i} 2008, 51, br. 111 - (t. i. br. 448): 366-367. godina)\" — na nivou poda JZ dela prostorije otvorene ka ulaznom prostoru peristila (stariji iskop, Dnevnik)\n     - Bunar jama 5 (sonda 105): dno 195.96, kasnosrednjovekovna keramika; bunar sonda 80: kote 198.2–196.05, kasnosrednjovekovna zeleno glazirana keramika\n   - `medijana_baza/pdf/milosevic_vila.txt` (read lines 1530–1600; OCR partly broken Cyrillic but English summary readable) — CRITICAL for task 5 (hoard):\n     - \"horizon, for which is very important the hoard of money found in one of the rooms ... last horizon, from the villa with peristyle, can be dated to time of the money hoard in horeum. Maximum circulation of ... period, which coincided with invasion of the Huns and demolition of Mediana in year 441.\"\n     - \"Circulation of money begins to grow from 310 to 324 ... After that, between year 320 and 324 the money circulation declines, while new growth was recorded again in the 330-...\" (Constantine's stays at Naissus; sons at Podunavlje); \"Due to poor preservation of the coins, it is not possible to date to the particular year pieces from that period, but it is very likely that the circulation increased exactly during the Emperor's stay.\"\n     - \"bronze coin of crispus (324-330)\" listed under FINDS OF ROMAN COINS\n     - Bronze railing hoard ~250 m NW (already in base)\n   - `medijana_baza/baza_podataka.json` (grepped) — castellum aquae: \"novac Aurelijana, Konstantina, Konstancija II\" (kraj 3. – sredina 4. veka); nalaz \"novac (1970-e, pri konzervaciji mozaika): nijedan primerak mladji od 350. godine\" (argument da prijemni deo više nije funkcionisao posle 350, poverenje srednje); spisak literature: Janković-Mihaldžić 2001 (novac sa objekta B, Zbornik NN 10, 27-38), Petrović 1994 monografija\n   - `medijana_baza/sobe_sloj.json` (grepped) — w-9: novac 335-336 (sloj B, kota 198.75) + 271-275 (sloj C, 198.49); w-10: novac 355-361 ×4 (sloj B, 198.52–198.54)\n   - `medijana_baza/SINTEZA.md` (grepped, output persisted to file) — nalazi: bronza